  "design_notes": [
    "The table has no Strengths, Lead / Integ. or Throttle column: no strengths, no lead_days, no integ_days, and a throttle range only for the solid motor (\"can't throttle\" is stored as throttle_min 1 and throttle_max 1, like the fixed-thrust Kerolox Giant of 7.7).",
    "No contracts list: the design restricts no upper-stage engine (Appendix A shows Kerolox Vacuum and Hydrolox Vacuum offered in C1).",
    "Hypergolic Storable: \"+$2 M ground handling, +3 days\" are modifiers. The cost is added once per vehicle (not per engine); the days are stored as schedule_days because the design does not say whether they are lead or integration time.",
    "Solid Kick Motor: mass \"0.12 t (+2 t propellant fixed)\" is mass_t 0.12 and fixed_propellant_t 2; the motor ignores the tank-size vote. \"Can't shut down\" is the flag cannot_shut_down.",
    "engine_shutdown is listed for every engine, as in first_stage_engine.json. For the solid motor it stands for a loss of thrust: 8.4 has no failure mode of its own for a motor that cannot be shut down.",
    "Methalox Vacuum: \"large nozzle needs a bigger interstage\" has no mass: flag needs_bigger_interstage. Its row says \"New tech\" but, unlike the Methalox Full-Flow of 7.7, recommends no test.",
    "Hydrolox Vacuum: boil-off on long coasts is checked by rule 6.11 through the propellant, so it has no flag (as for the hydrolox first-stage engine).",
    "Section 6.8 weights Helium Shortage towards \"pressure-fed systems\", but the design labels no engine as pressure-fed, so no engine carries that anomaly weight.",
    "F25 (hypergolics) is the \"Did you know?\" line under the table; it is on the category and on the Hypergolic Storable engine."
  ],
